# 🎯 Interview Questions

### Q1. Why use Multi-Leader Replication?

- Higher write throughput
- Lower global latency
- Better availability across regions

---

### Q2. Why are write conflicts common?

Because multiple leaders can update the **same key simultaneously**, creating different valid versions of the data.

---

### Q3. Why is All-to-All topology most popular?

It has **no central bottleneck**, offers **better fault tolerance**, and allows direct synchronization between leaders.

---

### Q4. What is Clock Skew?

Clock Skew is the difference between clocks on different machines because no hardware clock is perfectly accurate.

---

### Q5. Why is Last Write Wins dangerous?

Because timestamps can be wrong due to **Clock Skew** and **NTP adjustments**, causing valid writes to be discarded permanently.

